Ritemark: Electron 43.8.3, the newest of the pinned VS Code's Electron line
Sprint 144 (R3, #515). VS Code 1.142 pins Electron 43.7.7 (Node 24.21.0).
This patch moves it to Electron 43.8.3 (Node 24.22.0, Chromium 150.0.7871.250
with its later security backports, and the eMudhra intermediate CA distrust of
43.8.1). When Electron publishes a 43.x whose Node is 24.22.1 or later (the
21 October 2026 Node security releases), this patch moves to it: the target
line and Electron's own SHASUMS256.txt for that release.

Three files, no source change:
- .npmrc: `target`, read by the build (build/lib/electronVersion.ts) for the
  Electron it downloads and by npm for native-module headers. Every 43.x has
  native-module ABI 148, so modules built against 43.7.7's headers (CI runs
  npm ci before patching) load on 43.8.x. `ms_build_id` names Microsoft's own
  Electron build and is read only with product.electronArtifactFeed, which
  Ritemark never sets, so it stays as it is.
- build/checksums/electron.txt: Electron's own SHASUMS256.txt for the release
  (byte for byte, plus the trailing newline VS Code's copy has), against which
  the build verifies every Electron download (validateChecksum).
- cgmanifest.json: the Electron and Node versions in the notices.

Delete this patch, do not rebase it, at the next VS Code update whose pin
carries this Electron or a newer one. The audit:
docs/development/releases/v2.1.0/sprint-144-release-harness/research/electron-node-audit.md

